  "worked_solution": "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A\u2261\\text{T}$ and $B\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(A\u2228\u00acB)\u2227\u00acA & \u2261\u00ac(\\text{T}\u2228\u00ac\\text{F})\u2227\u00ac\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac(\\text{T}\u2228\\text{T})\u2227\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac\\text{T}\u2227\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\u2227\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A\u2261\\text{F}$ and $B\u2261\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(A\u2228\u00acB)\u2227\u00acA & \u2261\u00ac(\\text{F}\u2228\u00ac\\text{T})\u2227\u00ac\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac(\\text{F}\u2228\\text{F})\u2227\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac\\text{F}\u2227\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\u2227\\text{T} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A\u2261\\text{F}$ and $B\u2261\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\u2227(B\u2227\u00acA) & \u2261\\text{F}\u2227(\\text{F}\u2227\u00ac\\text{F}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\u2227(\\text{F}\u2227\\text{T}) \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\u2227\\text{F} \\\\  & \u2261\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,\u00ac(A\u2228\u00acB)\u2227\u00acA\\,$ | $\\,A\u2227(B\u2227\u00acA)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $\u00ac(A\u2228\u00acB)\u2227\u00acA$ is logically equivalent to $A\u2227(B\u2227\u00acA),$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they differ in the third row. Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\u00ac(A\u2228\u00acB)\u2227\u00acA\u2262A\u2227(B\u2227\u00acA).\n$$",
